      "text": "We are given the equation \\(3^{2x^2 - 5x + 2} = 3^{2x^2 + 7x - 4}\\). Since the bases are the same, we can set the exponents equal to each other:\n\n\\[2x^2 - 5x + 2 = 2x^2 + 7x - 4.\\]\n\nNext, we simplify this equation by subtracting \\(2x^2\\) from both sides:\n\n\\[-5x + 2 = 7x - 4.\\]\n\nThen, we combine like terms by adding \\(5x\\) to both sides:\n\n\\[2 = 12x - 4.\\]\n\nNext, we add 4 to both sides:\n\n\\[6 = 12x.\\]\n\nFinally, we solve for \\(x\\) by dividing both sides by 12:\n\n\\[x = \\frac{6}{12} = \\frac{1}{2}.\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(x\\) that satisfies the equation is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}}\\).",
